186346101 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347912 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346951 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347912 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186347103 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347912 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347912 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347912 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186345771 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347912 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b15bb1c1-681b-5425-b17c-5396ce1536d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348409 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348409 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80539" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348409 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348409 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $u=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}$ is a non-zero vector that is orthogonal to the set $W={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}},$ find the value of $\\frac{b+c}{a}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186348409 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ff28c518-d713-5726-9541-4836cde2e6b1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348409 #edb/ref 1074 "The vector $u$ is orthogonal to the set $W$ if $u\\cdot {w}_{1}=0$ and $u\\cdot {w}_{2}=0.$ So, we need to solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {w}_{1}=0 \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $2$ pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd), so ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{5}{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{5}{x}_{3}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{5}{x}_{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{5}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=5$, we get the vector \n$\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain $a=-1,$ $b=-2,$ and $c=5.$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{b+c}{a}=\\frac{-2+5}{-1}=-3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186348415 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347912 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348415 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80581" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348415 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348415 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the vector subspace $H=\\text{Span}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}}.$ Which of the following vectors belong to ${H}^{⊥}?$\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186348415 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "105935bf-05fc-5973-9fd9-74c435a6a9b6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348415 #edb/ref 1074 "Let  $h=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.$ A vector  $v$ belongs to ${H}^{⊥}$ if $v$ is orthogonal to $h.$ So, we have to find the products ${v}_{i}\\cdot h$ for $i=1,2,3.$   \n\n- For ${v}_{1}$, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot h & =4\\cdot 1+(-5)\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-4)=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSo, ${v}_{1}\\in {H}^{⊥}.$\n\n- For ${v}_{2}$, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2}\\cdot h & =2\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 4+(-3)\\cdot (-4)=30\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSo, ${v}_{2}\\notin {H}^{⊥}.$\n\n- For ${v}_{3}$, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3}\\cdot h & =1\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 4+4\\cdot (-4)=-19\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${v}_{3}\\notin {H}^{⊥}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${v}_{1}$  only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186393085 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393086 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393085 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393087 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393085 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393088 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393085 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393089 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393085 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393090 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393085 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393085 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393085 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186393088 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393085 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "98103ba7-7941-593f-8c55-fa6f21186d7c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393086 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393086 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393086 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6ae2689b-03da-5b4a-8bd9-e03a7a3d536c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393087 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393087 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393087 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2c523036-0297-53fb-8cf4-0a2347f12c7d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393088 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393088 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393088 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e5ddb235-9955-5a27-87c5-3f2c81216912" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393089 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393089 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393089 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "56996c07-885b-5b0d-8973-e1ca5a8ac3fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393090 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393090 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393090 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "81374ca6-2fbe-5ee7-a0ba-75942ffe6258" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186408166 #edb/ref 10 :answer-field.type/checkbox #edb/ref 175